s (grades, etc.) without the student’s consent and a signed FERPA waiver. Mission As a part of the Division of Student Success, Well-Being, and Belonging (SSWBB), the Dean of Student Office aims to foster a culture of belonging, self-advocacy, and care through programs, resources, and support. Learning Goals Meaningful Connections Contribution to Self and Community Professional Growth and Success Belonging Well-being Trauma-informed Care We approach care for our community through a trauma-informed lens, as we seek to understand the multitude of experiences and circumstances that affect students and their success inside and outside the classroom. 7916 Williamson Road Roanoke, VA 24020 800-456-9595 540-362-6000 huadm@hollins.edu Resources About Library Campus Store Security News For Media INFO FOR YOU First Year Students International Students Parents & Families Enrolled Students Alumnae/i Faculty & Staff Community Job Openings Events Campus Map & Directions The Roanoke Valley Staff Directory my.Hollins Privacy Policy Policies Title IX Accessibility Accreditation Notice of Non-Discrimination and Equal Opportunity"
